#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221119 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ccbf6e21-8dcb-5237-8c31-2a499858f973" :knowledge-point/title "Computing One Step Using the Trapezoidal Method"}] :question/id #uuid "5399454b-0691-5cb3-884f-26af4ca52f62" :question/math-academy-id "e-21671" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n$y' = 2x - y, \\qquad y(1) = 0$\nUse the trapezoidal method with one step to approximate $y\\!\\left(\\dfrac43\\right)$, rounded to two decimal places." :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\ny' = f(x,y), \\qquad y(a) = c\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $\\Delta x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\Delta y = \\dfrac12(y' + y'_\\text{new}) \\cdot \\Delta x\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\ny'_\\text{new} = f(x_\\text{new}, y_\\text{new})\n$$\n\nevaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, since we want to find the value of $y$ at\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac43\n$$\n\nwe will use a step size of\n\n$$\n\\Delta x = \\dfrac43 - 1 = \\dfrac13\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the trapezoidal method. In general, $\\Delta y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nΔy &= \\frac{1}{2}(y^{′} + y_{new}^{′}) \\cdot Δx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(2x - y + (2x_{new} - y_{new})) \\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{6}(2x - y + 2x_{new} - y_{new}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{6}(2x - y + 2x_{new}) - \\frac{1}{6}y_{new}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into\n\n$$\ny_\\text{new} = y + \\Delta y{:}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny_{new} &= y + Δy \\\\\ny_{new} &= y + \\frac{1}{6}(2x - y + 2x_{new}) - \\frac{1}{6}y_{new} \\\\\ny_{new} &= \\frac{1}{6}(2x + 2x_{new} + 5y) - \\frac{1}{6}y_{new}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve for the general formula for $y_\\text{new}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{7}{6}y_{new} &= \\frac{1}{6}(2x + 2x_{new} + 5y) \\\\\ny_{new} &= \\frac{1}{7}(2x + 2x_{new} + 5y)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is\n\n$$\nx_\\text{new} = 1 + \\dfrac13 = \\dfrac43\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny_{new} &= \\frac{1}{7}(2x + 2x_{new} + 5y) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{7}(2 \\cdot 1 + 2 \\cdot \\frac{4}{3} + 5 \\cdot 0) \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3} \\\\\n&\\approx 0.67\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\ny\\!\\left(\\dfrac43\\right) \\approx 0.67\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221120 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "78599a22-23ff-5b95-8305-fc40fd3bf548" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a General Update Formula for the Trapezoidal Method"}] :question/id #uuid "62a1e90b-05a5-5828-abe0-fa5cbb4c1c1a" :question/math-academy-id "e-21672" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n$y' = 3x^2 - 2y, \\qquad y(3) = -1$\nThe trapezoidal method is applied with step size $\\Delta x = 4$. Find the general formula for the new $y$ value, $y_\\text{new}$, in terms of the current values $x$ and $y$, and the new value $x_\\text{new}$." :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\ny' = f(x,y), \\qquad y(a) = c\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $\\Delta x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\Delta y = \\dfrac12(y' + y'_\\text{new}) \\cdot \\Delta x\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\ny'_\\text{new} = f(x_\\text{new}, y_\\text{new})\n$$\n\nevaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn this example, $\\Delta y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nΔy &= \\frac{1}{2}(y^{′} + y_{new}^{′}) \\cdot Δx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(3x^{2} - 2y + (3(x_{new})^{2} - 2y_{new})) \\cdot 4 \\\\\n&= 6x^{2} + 6x_{new}^{2} - 4y - 4y_{new}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into\n\n$$\ny_\\text{new} = y + \\Delta y{:}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny_{new} &= y + Δy \\\\\ny_{new} &= y + 6x^{2} + 6x_{new}^{2} - 4y - 4y_{new} \\\\\ny_{new} &= 6x^{2} + 6(x_{new})^{2} - 3y - 4y_{new}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for the general formula for $y_\\text{new}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5y_{new} &= 6x^{2} + 6(x_{new})^{2} - 3y \\\\\ny_{new} &= \\frac{1}{5}(6x^{2} + 6(x_{new})^{2} - 3y)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221121 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe0a8062-1387-5dd7-a568-0b0a6c4d04c6" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Two Steps Using the Trapezoidal Method"}] :question/id #uuid "d387bb78-9df1-5551-9e1e-5a4745c5b731" :question/math-academy-id "e-21673" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n$y' = 4x - y, \\qquad y(0) = 0$\nUse the trapezoidal method with two steps to approximate $y(1)$ and $y(2)$, rounded to two decimal places." :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\ny' = f(x,y), \\qquad y(a) = c\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $\\Delta x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\Delta y = \\dfrac12(y' + y'_\\text{new}) \\cdot \\Delta x\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\ny'_\\text{new} = f(x_\\text{new}, y_\\text{new})\n$$\n\nevaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, note that we are given $y(0)$ and asked to find $y(2)$. The distance from $x=0$ to $x=2$ is $2$, and since we are asked to use two steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\n\\Delta x = \\dfrac{2-0}2 = 1\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the trapezoidal method. In general, $\\Delta y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nΔy &= \\frac{1}{2}(y^{′} + y_{new}^{′}) \\cdot Δx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}((4x - y) + (4x_{new} - y_{new})) \\cdot 1 \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(4x + 4x_{new} - y) - \\frac{1}{2}y_{new}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into\n\n$$\ny_\\text{new} = y + \\Delta y{:}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny_{new} &= y + Δy \\\\\ny_{new} &= y + \\frac{1}{2}(4x + 4x_{new} - y) - \\frac{1}{2}y_{new} \\\\\ny_{new} &= \\frac{1}{2}(4x + 4x_{new} + y) - \\frac{1}{2}y_{new}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve for the general formula for $y_\\text{new}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{3}{2}y_{new} &= \\frac{1}{2}(4x + 4x_{new} + y) \\\\\ny_{new} &= \\frac{1}{3}(4x + 4x_{new} + y)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to calculate our approximations of $y(1)$ and $y(2)$.\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nFrom the initial conditions, we have\n\n$$\nx=0, \\qquad y=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is\n\n$$\nx_\\text{new} = x + \\Delta x = 0 + 1 = 1\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny_{new} &= \\frac{1}{3}(4x + 4x_{new} + y) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}(4 \\cdot 0 + 4 \\cdot 1 + 0) \\\\\n&= \\frac{4}{3} \\\\\n&\\approx 1.33\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nFrom the previous step, we have\n\n$$\nx=1, \\qquad y=1.33\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is\n\n$$\nx_\\text{new} = x + \\Delta x = 1 + 1 = 2\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny_{new} &= \\frac{1}{3}(4x + 4x_{new} + y) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}(4 \\cdot 1 + 4 \\cdot 2 + 1.33) \\\\\n&\\approx 4.44\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\ny(1) \\approx 1.33, \\qquad y(2) \\approx 4.44\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221900 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "78599a22-23ff-5b95-8305-fc40fd3bf548" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a General Update Formula for the Trapezoidal Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a789ead-1996-5af0-bc6d-d79ed5e1eb0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{new} = \\frac{y + e^{x_{new}}}{1 + 3x_{new}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220343} {:answer/id #uuid "bba6ba21-e81a-5d22-9fe0-a1e38445adaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{new} = \\frac{e^{x} + e^{x_{new}} + 2y}{2 - 3x_{new}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220344} {:answer/id #uuid "e6d5aab4-3054-5960-a074-aa69ad5ecdf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{new} = \\frac{e^{x} + e^{x_{new}} - 3xy + 2y}{2 + 3x_{new}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220345} {:answer/id #uuid "ed5dca78-c307-56a0-a32c-61f642cbb594" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{new} = \\frac{e^{x} + e^{x_{new}} - 3xy + y}{1 + 3x_{new}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220346} {:answer/id #uuid "0477ea03-e274-5524-a82f-8a1a904c9f8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{new} = \\frac{e^{x} + e^{x_{new}} - 3xy - 2y}{2 - 3x_{new}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6d5aab4-3054-5960-a074-aa69ad5ecdf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{new} = \\frac{e^{x} + e^{x_{new}} - 3xy + 2y}{2 + 3x_{new}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220345} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4938036-0b32-5e6e-95d3-042a28fc1cd5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220342}] :question/id #uuid "a6f655de-63db-57ed-a4b5-8a5ccc3c3a89" :question/math-academy-id "q-333386" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$y^{′} = e^{x} - 3xy, y(-2) = 3$\nThe trapezoidal method is applied with step size $Δx = 1$. Find the general formula for the new $y$ value, $y_{new}$, in terms of the current values $x$ and $y$, and the new value $x_{new}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221946 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ccbf6e21-8dcb-5237-8c31-2a499858f973" :knowledge-point/title "Computing One Step Using the Trapezoidal Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ecdd02c9-756f-5641-8900-9d6178d3fad7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "− 7.77" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220655} {:answer/id #uuid "4fe6f2db-ca7b-5538-bda2-79e4604ba76c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220656} {:answer/id #uuid "502eaf14-8a1a-5666-9a19-e5c14d9b39e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "− 6.34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220657} {:answer/id #uuid "65e89271-23f1-5109-bb51-24788b9cc527" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220658}] :answer-field/id #uuid "08733dc5-d9bd-53d6-a342-1c132cf6db66" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220654}] :question/id #uuid "58e